# Project: [ProductName] — Garment Manufacturing & Retail System (Ethiopia)

## Stack
Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Prisma + PostgreSQL,
Recharts, Zod + React Hook Form, NextAuth (role-based auth).

## Design tokens (TextilePro light — apply via CSS variables / Tailwind theme)
- bg-page: #F3F5FA, bg-surface/card: #FFFFFF
- primary accent: #5B5CE2 (hover #4849C9) — primary buttons, active nav item, focus rings
- secondary accent: #4F6EF7 — links, secondary actions
- status colors: success #22A06B, warning #D97706, danger #E5484D
- text: #0F1B33 headings, #6B7289 muted secondary text; on-primary #FFFFFF
- font: Inter. Rounded-xl cards, soft borders, light card shadow, 8px spacing scale.

## Layout skeleton
Persistent collapsible left sidebar with grouped nav sections (ACTION CENTER, NAVIGATE,
PRODUCTION, INVENTORY, ACCOUNTING, ADMINISTRATION, ACCESS CONTROL, SYSTEM). Top bar:
global search, notification bell, theme toggle, user profile menu. Standard page pattern:
title + short description → KPI card row → charts/tables below.

## Data model (Prisma — core entities, keep schema consistent with these names)
User, Role, Branch, RawMaterial, CapitalAsset, Supplier, StockMovement, Product,
ProductVariant, BillOfMaterial, PriceHistory, ProductionOrder, ProductionOutput, Employee,
FinishedGoodsStock, StockTransfer, Sale, SaleItem, Payment, Customer, AuditLog,
Notification, Approval.

## Coding conventions
- All money values in ETB, formatted with thousands separators (e.g. ETB 24,028.85).
- Any stock-affecting operation (BOM deduction, sale, transfer, adjustment) MUST be a
  single DB transaction. Never allow partial writes or silent negative stock — surface a
  clear error/warning instead.
- Folder pattern: app/(module)/page.tsx = list view, app/(module)/[id]/page.tsx = detail,
  app/(module)/new/page.tsx = create/edit form.
- Shared primitives in components/ui (shadcn); domain-specific components grouped under
  components/(module-name).
- All forms validated with a Zod schema in lib/validations/(module).ts, wired through
  React Hook Form.
- Prefer Next.js server actions for mutations over client-side fetch calls where possible.
- Reuse existing components/patterns already in the codebase before creating new ones.

## Rules for how you (Cursor) should work on this repo — token efficiency
- Only read/edit files relevant to the current task. Do not scan or refactor unrelated
  modules "while you're in there."
- For any non-trivial feature, first output a short plan (files to touch, schema changes,
  new components) and wait for confirmation before writing code.
- Keep changes scoped to what was asked. If you notice an unrelated issue, mention it
  briefly at the end rather than fixing it inline.
- Assume the person will commit after each working feature — you don't need to hold
  earlier uncommitted context in mind once a feature is confirmed working.
